# iGait dev shell.
#
# This file is intentionally tiny. It wires up two things:
#
#   1. `use flake` — drops you into the Nix dev shell (bw, jq, docker, etc.).
#   2. `dotenv_if_exists .env` — sources the .env written by `/igait-environment`
#      (Claude Code slash command) so Vaultwarden-sourced secrets are available
#      in your shell. Safe to run before that file exists: direnv no-ops.
#
# Secret materialisation itself does NOT happen here — it lives in the slash
# command so that re-auth to Vaultwarden is a conscious, on-demand action
# rather than something that fires on every `cd`.
#
# After a Vaultwarden rotation: re-run `/igait-environment`, then `direnv reload`.

use flake
dotenv_if_exists .env
